<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46708" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭper -fīo</span></b> ,
			fĭĕri, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to be over and
			above</i>, <i>to be left</i>, <i>to
				remain</i> (very rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not in Cic.): edepol te vocem (ad cenam)
					libenter, si superfiat locus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ep. 3, 2, 10</span></i>
			; 
			<i><span class="en">id. Mil.
				2, 4, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Stich. 4, 2, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Trin.
				2, 4, 108</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae superfieri possunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 1, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
